  "eng-2006-p1|The writer describes the features of a 'cottage industry' as|remedying urban migration, available employment, simplicity of operations and affordable products|rural location, simplicity, local sourcing of raw materials and affordability|affordable energy sources, availability of marketing of products|availability of capital, high productivity, low capital demand and simplicity of operations": "comprehension",
  "eng-2006-p1|Which of the following statements is true according to the passage?|Urban workplaces are responsible for rural poverty and misery.|Providing work opportunities in the rural areas will lead to low productivity, illiteracy and poverty.|Rural work opportunities could reduce urban unemployment.|Urban workplaces absorb rural/urban migrants.": "comprehension",
  "eng-2006-p1|In the first sentence of the passage, the word 'work', used differently, can be explained as|industrial and earn|job and struggle|employment and insure|career and prepare": "comprehension",
  "eng-2006-p2|Which of the following best summarizes the argument in the passage?|There are three laudable though unequal ways of news presentation by a daily paper.|Press freedom is an important feature of a daily newspaper.|There are three obvious functions of a daily newspaper.|A good newspaper is that which is simple, logical and balanced in its news coverage.": "comprehension",
